  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This dependable, robust, vigorous large tree has large, deep red leaves which hold their color well throughout the summer. The ultimate height is 20-26 ft. (6-8 m). The large fiveto seven-lobed leaves are Acer moderately deeply divided with numerous sharp fine teeth on the margins. The short stout leafedged stalks are also red. New leaves emerge a bright color pink-red, changing to deep plum-red in the sum- The mer then gradually becoming purple-red with tree, green undertones. This tree tolerates full sun wide very well. The name honors the town in the an Netherlands where the nursery is located that introduced this plant."
  },
